  "facts": [
    "The Wuhan Zhuankou Yangtze River Bridge stretches 5.296 kilometers, featuring a 760‑meter cable‑stayed main span that crowns its twin‑tower steel box girder design across the Yangtze River, the bridge's main span measures 760 meters.",
    "Connecting the Caidian District on Wuhan's north shore to Xujiabao on the south bank, the bridge serves as a critical artery of the Wuhan Fourth Ring Road.",
    "Formerly dubbed Huangjiahu Yangtze River Bridge, the structure earned its current name after the Zhuankou area was developed, reflecting Wuhan's rapid urban expansion in the early 21st century."
